To solve this problem, we can use the concept of a Voronoi diagram. A Voronoi diagram partitions a plane into regions based on distance from points in a specific subset of the plane. For the given conditions, the optimal placement for the lookout point would be the centroid (average) of the coordinates of all the roses. This ensures that the maximum Manhattan distance to any rose is minimized.

